TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (CaddG) and add the 5th note as necessary.

TIP:  The song is all about bass and cadence.  The (C) has a "scratch" rhythm to it.  Play the (C/G) wherever you see the (C) by covering the the top string/3rd fret bass note <g>.  And emphasize the top three or four strings throughout.  (Notes may or may not transpose.)

TIP:  The (CaddG) will follow a (C).  If you're playing the (C/G) as suggested above swing the pinky off the top string to the 1st string/3rd fret.  Easy.
 
  
